=== SURVEY ===

Existing F4/F5 surface used by F6 (read-only inspection):

1. internal/ai/provider/mock/mock.go (UNTOUCHED in this slice)
   - exports type Mock + New(...) + WithDefault + WithHashOverride +
     WithPromptOverride + Chat + Stream + Embed + Name + Capabilities.
   - Already canonical-hash-keys requests via canonHash(req).
   - F6 needs FIFO sequencing per-golden but the F6 prompt's allowed
     list names ONLY canned.go, not mock.go. Solution: a wrapper.

2. internal/ai/dispatch/dispatch.go
   - Run(ctx, req) loops: chat → forward delta → if no tool_calls
     return → process tool calls → append → next iter (lines 211–252
     of the F4 commit).
   - Multi-turn goldens (tool_call_then_answer) therefore need 2
     canned replies in sequence: turn 1 emits tool_calls, turn 2
     emits final assistant content with finish_reason=stop.

3. internal/ai/strategy/strategy.go
   - Strategy interface = { ID(), Build(StrategyInput) (BuiltPrompt,error),
     Context(ctx, in) (ContextPayload, error) }.
   - F6's GenericStrategy adapter satisfies this directly from the
     goldens.yaml feature header (system_prompt + tool list) so a
     feature can be eval'd before its real Strategy lands in U1+.

4. internal/ai/features/registry.go
   - Centrally lists every registered FeatureID (chatbot-llm is the
     first one, registered in F1+F4). F6 does NOT mutate the registry —
     goldens are discovered by walking
     internal/ai/strategies/<feature>/goldens.yaml.

5. internal/ai/tools/registry.go
   - Tool registry already enforces a per-feature whitelist + Mutates()
     gating + Confirm() prompts for mutating tools. F6 stub tools
     declare a permissive object schema and a no-op Execute that
     returns {"ok":true,"tool":"<name>"}; mutating stubs are auto-
     approved by an injected Confirm callback.

6. .gitignore
   - /.github/prompts/db-refactor/logs is gitignored, so the slice
     log is committed with `git add -f`. (This matches F0..F5.)

7. Pre-existing strategies/ directory: NONE. F6 creates it.

8. yaml.v3: already a transitive dep (used by k8s libs). F6 promotes
   it to a direct dep by importing it from canned.go + golden.go +
   schema-check tool. `go mod tidy` will write that line + its
   own indirect chain (kr/pretty, kr/text, rogpeppe/go-internal,
   gopkg.in/check.v1) into go.mod / go.sum.

