=== CHANGES ===

PRODUCTION CODE (new files):

  internal/ai/provider/mock/canned.go
      SequencedMock wrapper around mock.Mock + LoadCannedFile YAML
      loader + CannedReply / CannedToolCall / CannedFile wire types.
      Embeds *Mock so Name/Capabilities/Embed/WithHashOverride/
      WithPromptOverride/WithDefault all pass through unchanged.
      Overrides Chat + Stream to consume the FIFO sequence first;
      falls through to the embedded Mock on exhaustion. Validates
      finish_reason against {stop, tool_calls, length, content_filter}
      and rejects tool_calls with bad JSON arguments at load time.

  internal/ai/eval/doc.go
      Package doc + the I3/I4/I10 contract this package upholds.

  internal/ai/eval/types.go
      FeatureSpec, GoldenSet (with .Path), Golden, Expectations,
      Result, Mode (Fast | Full | Judged | Record).

  internal/ai/eval/golden.go
      LoadGoldenSet, LoadAllGoldens, GoldenSet.Validate (method).
      CannedDir + CannedFilePath helpers (golden-name → on-disk path).

  internal/ai/eval/strategy.go
      GenericStrategy: adapts a GoldenSet feature header into a
      strategy.Strategy without needing the feature's real Strategy
      implementation.

  internal/ai/eval/tools.go
      stubTool + stubRegistry: register read-only / mutating no-op
      tools per FeatureSpec.Tools and FeatureSpec.MutatingTools so
      the dispatcher's whitelist + confirm gate are satisfied.

  internal/ai/eval/runner.go
      RunSet + RunGolden orchestrators. Per golden:
        1. Load canned.yaml file via mock.LoadCannedFile.
        2. Build SequencedMock via mock.NewSequencedMock(mock.New(...)).
           Call SetSequence(cannedFile.ToReplies()).
        3. Build stub tool registry from FeatureSpec.
        4. Build CaptureWriter to record assistant deltas + tool calls.
        5. Build StrategyInput, pre-seed user message into History.
        6. Run Dispatcher.Run; wait for completion.
        7. applyExpectations: must_call_tools, must_not_call_tools,
           answer_must_contain, answer_must_not_contain. Each
           violation appends a human-readable string to Result.Reasons.
        8. If Mode == Judged: invoke judge.

  internal/ai/eval/judge.go
      Judge invoker: renders judge_prompt.tmpl with the user question,
      assistant answer, and rubric; calls a real provider with
      Temperature=0; parseJudgeReply tolerates JSON in surrounding
      prose via balanced-brace scan; populates Result.JudgeScore +
      Result.JudgeReason.

  internal/ai/eval/judge_prompt.tmpl
      Pinned judge template. Embeds seed={{.Seed}} (default 42).

  internal/ai/eval/report.go
      Text and JUnit XML reporters.

  cmd/ai-eval/main.go
      CLI entry. Flags --feature, --all, --root, --judge, --judge-model,
      --output, --record. Default mode = Fast. Exit 0 on all-pass,
      1 on any failure, 2 on CLI/IO error.

  tools/eval-schema-check/main.go
      Walks for goldens.yaml, calls eval.LoadGoldenSet (which calls
      Validate internally), reports per-file pass/fail, exits 1 on
      any failure.

  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/goldens.yaml
      5 starter cases per the prompt's Tasks #6:
        - range_question         (happy path, no tool call)
        - tool_call_battery      (single tool call → stop)
        - tool_call_then_answer  (tool call → assistant final answer)
        - refusal                (out-of-scope user, polite refuse)
        - ambiguous              (clarifying question)
      Tools declared: query_battery_status, query_vehicle_count,
      list_recent_drives, create_alert (mutating).

  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/canned/range_question.yaml
  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/canned/tool_call_battery.yaml
  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/canned/tool_call_then_answer.yaml
  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/canned/refusal.yaml
  internal/ai/strategies/chatbot-llm/canned/ambiguous.yaml
      One canned reply file per golden. tool_call_battery and
      tool_call_then_answer carry 2-reply sequences (tool_call → stop).

  .github/workflows/ai-eval.yml
      3 jobs:
        - fast    on PR — make ai-eval-fast, advisory (continue-on-error)
        - full    on push to main — make ai-eval-full, blocking,
                  publishes ai-eval.junit.xml as artifact
        - judged  nightly cron — make ai-eval-judged, gated on
                  JUDGE_PROVIDER + JUDGE_API_KEY secrets, skipped if
                  either is missing.

TESTS (new files):

